{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ישאו</b> — the meaning: for when the king judges justice, peace increases in the land." "And the meaning of <b>הרים</b> — that there is no settlement there." "And the meaning of <b>בצדקה</b> — on account of justice the mountains and hills will bear peace, in the manner of Baal Peor. And some say: כי בצדקה, like: שלום."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {2 "The comparison to Baal Peor is cryptic as in the source; Ibn Ezra appears to reference the hills of Peor as a scriptural example of mountains associated with a location or event, but the argument is left compressed and obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:58.513505101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}